    /**
     * Add-ons never offered to the owner (hidden_addons of the coverage map); installed_addons()
     * leaves them out, so they never reach the model.
     *
     * @return array
     */
    public static function hiddenAddons()
    {
        return array( 'blank', 'custom-javascript' );
    }

    /**
     * Descriptions of the read tools, keyed by tool name: what a tool returns and its arguments.
     * The tool schema carries it; the prompt has no second copy.
     *
     * @return array
     */
    public static function readTools()
    {
        return array(
            'get_settings' => 'Current value of each requested option and the values allowed on this installation. `allowed` is a list, a grid {grid: {from, to, step, also}} (times, durations), a range {min, max, step} or absent (text, colour, address — see the card). `allowed_depends` names options the list was computed from: if your proposal changes one of them, the list is not final — plan by the card\'s Constraints. `unavailable: <add-on>` — the control exists only with that add-on active; the value does not act on this site. `allowed_codes` — codes a text option may use. keys (list of string) — Option names.',
            'find_appointments' => 'Bookings as the Appointments page lists them, one row per customer of an appointment (a group appointment gives several rows with the same `id`; group them by `id`). Filters combine with AND; without `from` / `to` — today to today + 7 days by start, site time zone. `staff_id` (one) and `staff_ids` both narrow by staff; `service_ids` 0 = an appointment with its own (Custom) service; `location_ids` 0 = without location; `status` takes the slugs of the statuses, own statuses included (list_custom_statuses); `timeless: true` lists tasks without a time (Tasks add-on) and ignores the dates; `search` matches the id, booking number, customer name, phone, email, staff and service, like the page search. Rows are sorted by start. At most `limit` rows (default 50, up to 200): when `total_found` is greater than `returned` the list was cut — say how many you show of how many and narrow the filter; to count, use `total_found` or get_dashboard_summary, never the rows. Times are in the site time zone (`time_zone`), `duration` in SECONDS (extras included). An appointment without customers is one row with `booking_id`, `customer` and `status` null. `payment` null — no payment attached. `online_meeting` is the provider only, never a link. `location_id` is absent without the Locations add-on; `rating` is absent without the Ratings add-on. A staff member sees only their own appointments. Details of one appointment (custom fields, files, customer time zone, why a status) — get_appointment. staff_id? (integer) — One staff member (id from list_staff). Same as staff_ids with one id. staff_ids? (list of integer) — Staff members; empty — every staff member the user may see. from? (string) — YYYY-MM-DD, start date, site time zone. Default today. to? (string) — YYYY-MM-DD, inclusive. Default from + 7 days. timeless? (boolean) — Tasks without a time (Tasks add-on); from / to are ignored. service_ids? (list of integer) — Ids from list_services; 0 = own (Custom) service. customer_id? (integer) — Id from find_customers. Never guess it from a name. location_ids? (list of integer) — Ids from list_locations; 0 = without location. status? (list of string) — Status slugs: pending, approved, cancelled, rejected, waitlisted, done, own statuses. created_from? (string) — YYYY-MM-DD, date the booking was made. created_to? (string) — YYYY-MM-DD, inclusive. source? (frontend|backend) — backend — created in wp-admin; frontend — everything else: the booking form, the AI chat and also bookings that staff add in the staff cabinet or the mobile app (so it does not prove the customer booked). search? (string) — Free text limit? (integer)',
            'get_appointment' => 'One appointment in full, for "why is it Pending", "what was ordered", "who is in the group": time, staff (with their own time zone, null = the site\'s), service (category, duration in SECONDS, capacity) or the appointment\'s own Custom service, location, internal note, online meeting provider, when and where it was created, and `bookings` — every customer of the appointment with contacts (name, phone, email, customer group), status and when it last changed (`status_changed_at`, null = never changed after booking; a value ≈ `created_at` means the payment step switched the status at the booking itself), `source` (backend — created in wp-admin; frontend — everything else: the form, the AI chat and bookings staff add in the staff cabinet or the mobile app, so it does not prove the customer booked), places, units, extras, custom fields with their labels, the names of uploaded files, notes, series and package, the customer\'s time zone at booking and the payment. `location` is absent without the Locations add-on; `files` is absent without the Files add-on. To explain a status, combine `status`, `source`, `payment.status` and `customer.group_id` with get_settings (bookly_appointment_default_status, bookly_successful_payment_appointment_status) and the customer group (list_customer_groups). Times are in the site time zone (`time_zone`). An id that does not exist or belongs to another staff member answers `not_found`. appointment_id (integer) — The `id` from find_appointments. Never a customer name.',
            'find_free_slots' => 'Free start times for a service as the admin\'s New appointment wizard finds them: every staff member who performs it, with their working hours, special days, days off, existing busy appointments, padding, events, external calendars and capacity taken into account. The admin\'s search has NO minimum time before booking but stops at the same booking horizon as the forms (a horizon under 10 days is searched for 10 days), so a customer on the booking form or in the chat may see fewer times (say so when the owner compares). Needs `service_id`, or `duration` (SECONDS) for an appointment with its own service; without either, ask which service — for "who works / is free on Friday" without a service use get_staff_day. `days` is the number of days WITH free times to collect (1–7, default 3) from `date_from` (default today): fully booked days are skipped, not counted. Per day and staff member `free` lists start times in the site time zone (`time_zone`); a run of starts every `step_minutes` is written as one range "10:00-12:30" (10:00, 10:30, … 12:30 with a 30-minute step). `waiting_list` — times that are full but take a waiting-list entry (Waiting List add-on), absent when there are none. For a group service a free time may already have customers in it while places remain. `time_from` / `time_to` only filter the answer. `next_date` — where to continue for more days, null when the search reached the booking horizon; `timed_out: true` — the search stopped on its time limit before collecting `days` days (continue from `next_date`). A staff member sees only themselves. service_id? (integer) — Id from list_services. duration? (integer) — SECONDS, for an appointment with its own (Custom) service instead of service_id. date_from? (string) — YYYY-MM-DD, site time zone. Default today. days? (integer) — Days with free times to collect. staff_ids? (list of integer) — Only these staff members; empty — every performer of the service. location_id? (integer) — Id from list_locations (Locations add-on). persons? (integer) — Places for a group service. units? (integer) — Duration multiplier of a service with variable duration. extras? (object) — {extra_id: quantity}, ids from get_service_extras; their duration counts when the Extras step allows it. time_from? (string) — HH:MM, only times from it. time_to? (string) — HH:MM, only times up to it.',
            'get_staff_day' => 'Whether staff members work on given days and what is already booked, without a service — for "who works / is free on Friday", "is Peter in on 1 November". Per day and staff member: `hours` — the working hours that apply that day, in the shape of a schedule day {start, end, breaks} or "off"; `hours_from` — schedule (the weekly schedule), special_day (Special Days add-on) or day_off (a day off in the staff member\'s Days off; it beats the weekly hours, but a special day WITH hours beats a day off); `busy` — appointments in statuses that hold time (pending, approved, waitlisted and own statuses marked Busy; an appointment without customers too) and events (Events add-on); `free` — the working time left after breaks and busy, as intervals. `free` is NOT a list of bookable times: a service also needs its duration, padding and capacity, and events of external calendars (Google, Outlook) are not in `busy` — for exact times call find_free_slots with the service. All times are "HH:MM" in the site time zone (`time_zone`); `staff_time_zone` is the staff member\'s own zone (null = the site\'s), their hours are already converted - so after the conversion a time can fall before midnight ("-01:00" = 01:00 of the previous day) or after 24:00 (next day). `busy[].status` is the status of the appointment\'s customers: for a group appointment all of them comma-separated ("approved,pending"), null for an appointment without customers (events have no status). Without `staff_ids` — every staff member who is not archived. `days` 1–7 from `date` (default 1). With `location_id` the hours of that location (Locations add-on, custom schedule). A staff member sees only themselves. date (string) — YYYY-MM-DD, site time zone. days? (integer) staff_ids? (list of integer) — Ids from list_staff; empty — every staff member who is not archived. location_id? (integer) — Id from list_locations; the staff member\'s schedule for that location.',
            'get_dashboard_summary' => 'The numbers of Bookly > Dashboard for a period, counted exactly as the dashboard counts them: for `current` and the comparison period `previous` — appointments (bookings) in total and by status, revenue, customers (total, new — their first matching booking is in the period, returning) and `sales` ({total, tickets, packages, gift_cards}: numbers of event tickets, packages and gift cards sold; a key is present only for a product the site has, `total` is their sum; null when the site sells none of these). How it counts: done counts as approved, own statuses marked Busy as approved and Free as cancelled, waitlisted separately; revenue is paid plus later payments of the bookings in the period WITHOUT regard to the payment status (refunded and pending online payments are included), plus packages, tickets and gift cards sold without an appointment by payment date. `based_on` start_date counts by appointment date (default here), created_at by booking date — say which one you used; the owner\'s dashboard may be set to the other. With `breakdown: true` (Pro) also the table "Appointments by staff and service": one row per staff × service pair with activity; a payment for several services counts in full in each pair, so the rows add up to more than `breakdown_total.revenue`; `breakdown_total.sales_revenue` is the part of the dashboard revenue no row holds. `breakdown` and `breakdown_total` are absent when not asked; without Pro they are absent and `unavailable` says `breakdown: pro`. Amounts in the site currency. Administrators only. from (string) — YYYY-MM-DD, site time zone. to (string) — YYYY-MM-DD, inclusive. based_on? (start_date|created_at) compared_to? (previous_period|previous_year) staff_ids? (list of integer) — Ids from list_staff (archived included); empty — all. service_ids? (list of integer) — Ids from list_services; 0 = own (Custom) service; empty — all. breakdown? (boolean) — Add the staff × service table (Pro).',
            'list_services' => 'All services in the order of the booking form (position): id, title, type, category, visibility, price, duration in SECONDS, tags. Use the ids in every service action; the order of the list is the order sync_services_order takes.',
            'get_service' => 'One service in the shape the service actions take: `service` — the fields of set_service (units: SECONDS for duration, slot_length, padding, min times; days for package_life_time and the occupancy period); `staff_ids` — Providers (set_service_staff); `staff_preference_order`; `steps` — set_service_sub_services; `tags`; `schedule` — set_service_schedule (service-schedule add-on). `allowed` — the values the dialog offers on this site for list fields; `unavailable: {field: add-on}` — fields whose control needs an inactive add-on; `not_for_type` — fields the dialog does not show for this service type. service_id (integer) — Id from list_services.',
            'get_service_extras' => 'The extras of one Simple service in the order of the Extras tab (and of the booking form step), in the shape set_service_extra takes: id, title, price (the currency of the site), duration in SECONDS (0 = OFF), min_quantity, max_quantity, attachment_id (null = no picture), position, and next to them `hidden` (max_quantity 0 — clients do not see the extra, the admin does) and `appointments` (customer appointments that have the extra chosen). `allowed.duration` is the list the Duration dropdown offers (OFF and multiples of the time slot length up to 12 hours, seconds), `allowed.time_step_minutes` its step. `extras_step` says whether clients get the step at all and whether the extras\' duration counts: `enabled` (Show Extras step), `after_step_time` (the step comes after the time) — with the step after the time, or not shown, a duration set on an extra does not lengthen the visit. The list `extras` is empty when the service has no extras. Only Simple services have extras: for a service of another type the answer is the short `extras_tab: false` with its type; with the add-on inactive it is `unavailable`. service_id (integer) — Id from list_services.',
            'list_staff' => 'All staff members in the order of the booking form (position), archived included: id, full name, visibility (public / private / archive), staff category. The order of the list is the order sync_staff_order takes. Archived staff members cannot be added as Providers of a service. Details, services, schedule and special days of one staff member — get_staff.',
            'list_categories' => 'Service categories in the order of the booking form: id, name, info, position, number of services. The shape set_category takes.',
            'list_taxes' => 'Taxes (Taxes add-on): id, title, rate in percent, ids of the services the tax is applied to. The shape set_tax takes; service.taxes holds these ids.',
            'get_staff' => 'One staff member in the shape the staff actions take: `staff` — the fields of set_staff; `services` — the services they perform with their own price and capacity (set_staff_services); `schedule` — weekly hours and breaks (set_staff_schedule, set_staff_schedule_break); `special_days` — special days from today on (set_staff_special_day, Special Days add-on). `allowed` — what the dialog offers on this site: `services` lists every service the Services tab shows (package_of = the simple service of a package), `gateways`, `time_step_minutes`. `location_schedules` / `location_services` — locations with their own settings, which these actions do not change. `unavailable: {field: add-on}` — fields whose control needs an inactive add-on. staff_id (integer) — Id from list_staff.',
            'list_staff_categories' => 'Staff categories (Pro) in their order: id, name, info, position, number of staff members. The shape set_staff_category takes; staff.category_id holds these ids.',
            'list_locations' => 'Locations (Locations add-on) in their order (position): id, name, info, position and the ids of the staff members who work there (`staff_ids`). The shape set_location and sync_locations_order take; staff ids are the ids of list_staff. Without the Locations add-on (it needs Pro) the answer is the short `unavailable`.',
            'get_staff_locations' => 'The locations one staff member works in, with the three "own settings" switches of each pair, in the shape set_staff_locations and set_staff_location_settings take: `location_id`, `custom_services`, `custom_schedule`, `custom_special_days` (true = "Use custom settings" in this location, false = "Use default settings"); next to them `name` and `own_services` (how many services the staff member has with their own price in this location, kept even while the switch is off). The switches act only while the option "Custom settings for location" (bookly_locations_allow_services_per_location, get_settings) is enabled. `custom_special_days` is absent when the Special Days add-on is inactive (no such tab, the switch cannot be set). The list `locations` is empty for a staff member without locations. staff_id (integer) — Id from list_staff.',
            'get_service_special_days' => 'Special days of one service from today on (Special Days add-on; they act only with the Service Schedule add-on): date and hours — {date, start, end, breaks} or {date, off: true}. The shape set_service_special_day takes. `time_step_minutes` — the time grid. service_id (integer) — Id from list_services.',
            'list_custom_statuses' => 'Own appointment statuses (Custom Statuses add-on, needs Pro) in the order of the Order dialog: id, slug (the key options and filters refer to), name, busy (1 Busy — holds a place in the time slot, 0 Free — releases it), position, colour and the number of appointments that have the status now. The shape set_custom_status and sync_custom_statuses_order take; the default, successful-payment and auto-change options hold these slugs.',
            'get_cloud_stripe_metadata' => 'Custom metadata of Stripe Cloud payments (Settings → Payments → Stripe Cloud): whether the Stripe Cloud product is active, the two switches that show the list, the list itself and the codes a value may use. `metadata` is the shape set_cloud_stripe_metadata takes. Without an active product the list is not on the page and cannot be changed.',
            'find_payments' => 'Payments as the Payments page lists them (main payments only, newest first): id, date, method, customer, status and the amounts. Use it to find the payment id for complete_payment or set_payment_adjustment. Filters combine with AND. `search` matches the payment number, customer, staff, service, amounts and the order text, like the page search. There is no total over the result: sum the rows yourself and say how many were returned. search? (string) — Free text customer_id? (integer) staff_id? (integer) service_id? (integer) status? (list of completed|pending|rejected|refunded) type? (list of string) — Payment methods created_from? (string) — YYYY-MM-DD created_to? (string) — YYYY-MM-DD limit? (integer)',
            'get_payment' => 'One payment as its dialog shows it: method, status, total, tax, paid, additional payments by link (child_paid), what is still due, the order\'s appointments with their statuses, the manual adjustments with their index and whether the dialog would show the Complete payment button and the Tax field. `adjustments` is the shape set_payment_adjustment takes (index, reason, amount, tax). Amounts are in the site currency; the payment does not store a currency. payment_id (integer) — Id from find_payments. Never a customer name.',
            'get_cloud_account' => 'The Bookly Cloud account of this site as the Account, Billing and Products pages show it: whether the site is signed in, email, balance (US dollars), country, Auto-Recharge, support, weekly summary, invoice details and the products with their subscriptions. `weekly_summary`, `auto_recharge_limit` and `invoice` are the shapes set_cloud_account and set_cloud_invoice_details take. `auto_recharge`, `auto_recharge_limit` and `intervals` are present only while Auto-Recharge is on: no `auto_recharge` in the answer means Auto-Recharge is OFF (a fact, not unknown) and there is no cap to read or set; no `intervals` means the same — it is the list of periods (hours) the cap can take, so it exists only where the cap section is on the page. `voice.language` is the language of the voice that reads all phone-call notifications (the shape set_cloud_voice_settings takes: one of the 26 codes), `null` when Cloud returned none; no `voice` in the answer means the Voice product is not active on the account, so there is no language to read or set. A subscription\'s `usage` is the text of the Products page ("Tasks: 4 / 300", "Messages: 120 / 500" for WhatsApp, "AI answers: 120 / 500" for the AI products, in the trial "Tasks: unlimited in trial") or null. Not signed in — only `signed_in: false`: nothing of the account can be read or changed; products that work through the sign-in (SMS, WhatsApp, Voice, Stripe Cloud, the AI chat and the Admin assistant) do not work, while Cloud Cron, Zapier and the mobile app keep working with the keys stored on the site.',
            'list_notifications' => 'Notifications of one channel as the table lists them (email — Email Notifications → Notifications, sms — SMS Notifications → Notifications, voice — Voice Notifications → Notifications, whatsapp — WhatsApp Notifications → Notifications): id, name, active (1 Enabled, 0 Disabled), type with its title and `kind` (instant — sent at the event, scheduled — sent only while cron runs). `gateway` is email (default), sms, voice or whatsapp. `allowed` is what the dialog of that channel offers on this site: `types` — every type with its recipients, attachments and `timing_options` (values of settings.option the type may use; [] — no send time), `statuses` — values of Appointment status, `invoices` — whether Attach invoice exists (Invoices add-on active; always false for sms). The two channels offer different types: sms has no verify_email but verify_phone, its reminder, last appointment and agenda types need no Pro, and no sms type has attachments. voice offers the sms set (verify_phone yes, no staff_new_wp_user) and whatsapp the same without verify_phone (with staff_new_wp_user), neither has attachments. Notifications of a type this site does not offer are not listed (the table does not list them) and cannot be changed. One notification in full — get_notification; the codes its text may use — get_notification_codes. The WhatsApp message templates — list_whatsapp_templates. Voice and WhatsApp send only while the site is signed in to Bookly Cloud with the product active (get_cloud_account); the list itself is read from the site and exists regardless. gateway? (email|sms|voice|whatsapp) — Channel of the notifications to list.',
            'get_notification' => 'One notification (email, sms, voice or whatsapp) in the shape set_notification takes: `gateway`, name, active, subject, message (as stored), the recipient flags (1/0), custom_recipients as a list (email addresses, or phone numbers for sms, voice and whatsapp), the attachment flags and `settings` with every key the dialog stores (keys the type does not use hold their stored or default value and have no effect). Plus read-only `title` and `kind`. `settings.services.ids` and `settings.payment_statuses` are the current lists the action changes with add / remove; `payment_statuses` matters only for the Events new-ticket type, on every other type it holds the default Completed and is ignored ([[notification.payment_statuses]]). An sms, voice or whatsapp notification has no `subject` and no `attach_ics` / `attach_invoice` in the answer: such a message has no subject and no attachments, so their absence is not "empty" and cannot be set. A voice notification\'s `message` is the text the robot reads. A whatsapp notification has NO `message` in the answer — the stored value is only the position of the template in the Cloud list at the moment of saving (W-1), not a text — its message is `settings.whatsapp`: `template` (Meta name), `language`, `header` and `body` (the values of the variables {{1}}, {{2}}… in ascending order of the number; [] when the template has none), the shape the `whatsapp` argument of set_notification takes. `template_status` (whatsapp only) is the status of that template now in the Cloud list (APPROVED, PENDING, REJECTED, …) or `missing` when no template of that name and language is in the list; absent while the site is not signed in to Bookly Cloud with WhatsApp active. Only APPROVED templates send. notification_id (integer) — Id from list_notifications (either channel).',
            'get_notification_codes' => 'Codes ({name}) the text of a notification of this type may use on this site, with the description of each; `if` — the code may stand in {#if code} conditions. The set depends on the channel (`gateway`: email by default, sms, voice or whatsapp — voice and whatsapp use exactly the sms set; for whatsapp these are the codes a template variable may hold), the type and the active add-ons; image and logo codes exist only for email and work only when emails go out as HTML (bookly_email_send_as); {cancel_appointment} is email only (prints the bare URL in text). An sms text has none of the email-only codes: {company_logo}, {category_image}, {service_image}, {staff_photo}, {cancel_appointment}. `loops` — lists a text may iterate with {#each} and the codes of one item (written item.code). A code not in this answer is printed as nothing, so set_notification refuses it. type (string) — Type from list_notifications.allowed.types of the same gateway. gateway? (email|sms|voice|whatsapp) — Channel whose codes are listed. voice and whatsapp answer as sms.',
            'list_whatsapp_templates' => 'The WhatsApp message templates of the owner\'s Meta (WhatsApp Business) account as the Template list of the WhatsApp notification dialog shows them: `name`, `language` (Meta code, e.g. en_US), `status` (APPROVED, PENDING, IN_APPEAL, REJECTED, PENDING_DELETION, DELETED, DISABLED, PAUSED, LIMIT_EXCEEDED), the text of `header` (absent when the template has no text header) and `body`, the numbers of the variables in them (`header_variables`, `body_variables`: the distinct {{N}}, ascending — one value per number is what set_notification takes, in this order) and `usable`. A template is identified by its name AND language together (one name exists in several languages) — never by its position in this list: the order is Meta\'s and changes when templates are added or removed. Only `usable: true` templates can be put into a notification: status APPROVED and only text variables numbered {{1}}, {{2}}… in the text header and the body; a template with a media header (image, document, video), a URL button with a variable, or named variables {{name}} is `usable: false` and `reason` (absent when usable) says why (the notification dialog would let it be chosen, but Meta refuses what it receives). Templates are created, changed and approved only in Meta (WhatsApp Manager) — Bookly cannot do it and neither can the assistant. An empty `templates` list means the Meta account has none or the credentials of Bookly Cloud → WhatsApp → Settings are wrong or empty; they are not readable here (the access token is a secret). Not signed in to Bookly Cloud — {signed_in: false}; signed in but the WhatsApp product is not active — {product_active: false}; an error of Bookly Cloud or Meta — {error: "<message as it came>"}.',
            'list_sms_campaigns' => 'SMS campaigns as the Campaigns tab lists them, newest first: id, name, `status` (ready — saved without sending, no date; scheduled — has a send date; sending; completed; stopped), send_at (site time, null = Manual), the audience (preset key or custom), the number of recipients and, once sending has started, the results. `draft: true` marks the campaigns that set_sms_campaign may change — ready ones; a scheduled, sending, completed or stopped campaign is only read. The number of recipients of a ready preset campaign is counted as of now — the rule is applied again when the campaign is sent. Not signed in to Bookly Cloud — {signed_in: false}: the Campaigns tab does not open.',
            'get_sms_campaign' => 'One SMS campaign in the shape set_sms_campaign takes: name, text and `audience` (a preset {type: preset, key, params} or an own list {type: custom, filter}; a custom audience of an old campaign has `filter: null` — it is only a list). Plus the read-only state: `status`, send_at, and `recipients` — their number, the first 50 as the dialog\'s preview and, with `find`, the people whose name or phone contains that text (at most 50). For a preset `recipients.added_by_hand` lists the people added to the rule\'s result by hand and `recipients.excluded` the phone numbers taken out of it; for an own list the saved list is the recipients, the same changes are already part of it. The text is as stored, with {codes}. A campaign that has started (sending, completed, stopped) also has `results` — {queued, sent, failed}, its recipients are fixed; no `results` means nothing was queued yet. No `matches` means `find` was not given; no `added_by_hand` / `excluded` means the campaign is an own list (the changes by hand are part of its saved list) or nobody was added / taken out. `audience.params` holds the keys of that preset only (none for a custom audience). campaign_id (integer) — Id from list_sms_campaigns. find? (string) — Part of a name or a phone number to look for among the recipients; answers `matches`.',
            'list_sms_audiences' => 'What the New campaign dialog offers: the eight preset audiences (key, title, `phrase` with the {limits} the owner can change, the default limits, the ranges of each limit, how many people each gives with the defaults, and the ready-made text the dialog starts with), the own-list filter (what it can choose from) and the codes a campaign text may use. The preset counts are as of now. The keys of `defaults` and `limits` depend on the preset — each preset lists only its own. Use it before proposing a campaign: pick the preset by the owner\'s words, keep the defaults unless the owner names a limit.',
            'preview_sms_audience' => 'Who a campaign audience would reach right now, without saving anything: the number of recipients, the first 50 of them and the one with the longest name (the SMS for him is the longest). `audience` is the argument of set_sms_campaign. Use it to try limits ("a year instead of 90 days") before proposing. A preset is counted as of now and again when the campaign is sent; an own list is counted once and fixed when saved. audience (object) — A preset {type: preset, key, params} or an own list {type: custom, filter}; the shape of set_sms_campaign.audience.',
            'list_customer_groups' => 'Customer groups (Customer Groups add-on) and the settings for customers without a group, in the shape set_customer_group takes: per group id, name, description, appointment_status ("" = Default), discount (text: "10" or "10%"), skip_payment (0|1), gateways ("default" or the list of method ids) and the number of customers in it. `general_settings` — the same fields (no id, name, description) for customers without a group; `customers` there is how many customers have no group. `allowed` — what the dialog offers on this site: statuses and ids of the enabled payment methods.',
            'find_customers' => 'Find customers by a text: it is looked for in the id, full, first and last name, phone, email, tags (Pro) and the values of the customer\'s own fields, whichever columns the Customers table shows. Returns at most `limit` customers (default 20, up to 50) with `total` matches; empty search = the latest customers by id. Use it to get customer_id for get_customer and set_customer; never guess an id from a name — if several match, ask which one. search? (string) — Text to look for. Omit for the latest customers. limit? (integer)',
            'get_customer' => 'One customer in the shape set_customer takes: the fields of the customer dialog (name, phone, email, birthday, address parts, notes, group_id, tags, info_fields) plus read-only data: wp_user (the linked WordPress user), the number of appointments, `info_field_defs` (id, label, type, items of the customer\'s own fields — what info_fields values mean; a time field also has `delimiter`, the step of its times in minutes) and `allowed` (groups, name mode, address parts shown, phone format). Fields of an add-on that is not active are absent and listed in `unavailable`. customer_id (integer) — Id from find_customers.',
            'list_forms' => 'The saved modern booking forms (Bookly > Appearance; they need Pro), one entry per form: `id`, `type` (search-form, services-form, staff-form, tags-form, cancellation-confirmation, checkout-form, events-form, ai-assistant-form), `name`, `slug` (the word in the shortcode), `editable` (false for the kinds that no form action changes - checkout and events forms of other areas; an AI assistant form is editable: true and is changed by set_ai_form, not set_form), `shortcode` and `theme` (read-only: the name of the applied theme, "" = Default) and `settings` - the form\'s settings in the shape set_form takes, with the kind\'s defaults filled in for keys the owner never changed; `settings` holds only the keys the kind has. A list that is null shows everything (`services_list: null` - every service, also ones created later); `hidden_services` is a list of service ids; `details_fields_show` / `details_fields_order` hold field ids, widths are in twelfths of the row (the widths of custom-field items are left out). With `form_id` the entry also has `l10n` - all texts of that form by key (a group stays an object); set_form changes only keys that are there. Without args every form is listed; `type` narrows to one kind. `shortcode` is absent for kinds whose shortcode is not known, `settings` for forms with editable false. An ai-assistant-form has `settings` {main_color, question_bubble_color (null = follows main_color), answer_bubble_color, display_mode, show_avatars, assistant_knowledge, assistant_instructions} and, with form_id, `l10n` (the chat\'s texts, including the payment_system_<type> captions of the payment methods the form offers), and `payment_texts_used` - true only for the FIRST AI form (lowest id): the chat reads the payment method captions and the payment result texts from that form alone. The classic [bookly-form] is not a saved form - its settings are options (get_settings). Without Pro the answer is the short `unavailable`, except that ai-assistant-form entries (a core form kind) are still listed. Exactly: without Pro the answer is the list of AI assistant forms only; if the site has no AI form, or `type` is any other kind, or `form_id` is not an AI form, the answer is {unavailable: pro}. With Pro an unknown `form_id` gives {error: "form not found"}. type? (search-form|services-form|staff-form|tags-form|cancellation-confirmation|checkout-form|events-form|ai-assistant-form) — Only forms of this kind. form_id? (integer) — One form by id - then the entry also has `l10n`.'
        );
    }
}
